## 3. Daily Toolchain Inventory

Based on Atlassian's actual ML Platform stack: [End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202046686c7c93274f379403a2283d58293f/pages/6708596091/End-to-End+ML+Framework+Atlassian)

### 3.1 Experiment Tracking & Model Registry

| Tool | Role | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| **MLflow** (Databricks-hosted) | Experiment tracking, model registry, artifact storage | `mlflow.log_metric()`, `mlflow.log_param()`, `mlflow.<framework>.log_model()`, experiment comparison, model versioning/staging |
| **ML Registry (Tarot V3)** | Model registration, deployment tracking, lineage | Register model groups, version management, deployment configuration |
| **ML Lineage (Dreamcatcher)** | End-to-end traceability | Automatically captures workflow→dataset→model→deployment provenance |

Source: [MLflow Integration in Airlock Flows](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/xugc/pages/6659921772/MLflow+Integration+in+Airlock+Flows), [Introducing ML Lineage](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2025/12/11/6186798518/Introducing+ML+Lineage+End+to+End+Traceability+Across+the+ML+Platform)

### 3.2 Compute Orchestration & Training Infrastructure

| Tool | Role | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| **ML Fabric** (Kubernetes) | GPU-accelerated distributed training | PyTorchJob (Kubeflow), RayJob, multi-node DDP, H200/A10G/L40S GPUs |
| **ML Studio** (Databricks) | Workflow orchestration, notebook environment | DAG-based workflows (data prep → training → evaluation → packaging → registration) |
| **Argo Workflows** | Kubernetes-native ML pipeline orchestration | Replacing Databricks as orchestration layer for ML Fabric |
| **Karpenter** | GPU autoscaling | Elastic GPU provisioning on Kubernetes |
| **KAI Scheduler / Kueue** | Job queueing and fair-share scheduling | Queue management for GPU workloads across teams |

Source: [ML Orchestration Roadmap](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202091e93be306a64a9b8d5e1faf780e8820/pages/7013482971/ML+Orchestration+Roadmap+From+Databricks+to+ML+Fabric+on+Kubernetes), [ML Fabric Deep Dive](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/5854459593/ML+Fabric+Deep+Dive)

### 3.3 Feature Stores

| Tool | Role | Status |
|---|---|---|
| **MLFS** (in-house ML Feature Store) | Primary feature store — feature definition (Python DSL), materialization, online/offline serving, data governance | Long-term replacement for Tecton; supports UGC compliance |
| **Tecton** | Third-party feature store (being deprecated by Nov 2026) | Stream/batch feature engineering, online serving via DynamoDB |

Source: [MLFS & Tecton](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TCH1/pages/5576660473/MLFS+Tecton), [PSA: ML Platform is deprecating Tecton](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/blog/2025/12/03/6159139910/PSA+ML+Platform+is+deprecating+Tecton)

### 3.4 Model Serving & Inference

