## 2. Guardrails and Safety Checks

### 2.1 Responsible AI Review Framework

Atlassian's responsible AI framework operates through multiple layers:

**Responsible Tech Reviews:**
- Identify risk of bias within AI systems
- Rely on individual teams to put measures in place to mitigate bias
- Mandatory for new AI features before launch

**AI Safety Filters (Centralized Policy Filtering):**
- Check inputs against Atlassian's Acceptable Use Policy (AUP)
- Prompts violating the AUP return error messages
- Developed with safety datasets from synthetic data, open-source datasets, and internal/external feedback
- Diverse annotation teams to minimize individual or group bias

Sources: [9 — AI Safety & Responsible AI](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120201bc0c38992be4219ba741180eb8a6969/pages/7012229938/9+AI+Safety+Responsible+AI), [Bias Mitigation in AI](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~7120205eb410d339754170844dc040125b5093/pages/5716665200/Bias+Mitigation+in+AI)

### 2.2 Model Bias & Fairness Audits

**Pre-deployment requirements:**
- Define fairness goal up-front: who benefits, who could be harmed, which fairness metric to prioritize
- Slice metrics by group (region, cohort) alongside overall score
- Check error balance: compare false positives/negatives across groups
- Attempt mitigation: balanced sampling, re-weighting, calibrated thresholds, post-processing
- Human-in-the-loop for high-impact decisions, especially in early rollout
- Document in model card: purpose, data, limits, fairness results

**Red flags to catch:**
- Only overall accuracy reported; no group breakdowns
- "We removed sensitive fields, so we're fair" (proxies still leak)
- No data inventory or unclear licences
- No rollback plan or human-in-the-loop for high-impact decisions

Source: [AI fairness & data risks](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121eeecde7086e94a778d189b8b5d0a90f2/pages/5749449742/AI+fairness+data+risks)

### 2.3 Data Privacy & Compliance

**Data access controls by lifecycle phase:**
- **Experimental (Development):** Only access Plato Staging Source Tables for safe experimentation
- **Adhoc (Staging):** Access to Plato Production Source Tables for validation against real data
- **Released (Production):** Full production data access for real-time ML inference

**Privacy requirements:**
- PII scrubbing and data access controls
- PD scrubbing, de-identification, MRP for cross-tenant data
- DPIA/PIA completion
- Contractual data handling; default opt-out of training on customer data
- Encrypt prompts/outputs at rest and in transit

Source: [LDR: Restricting Production Data Access for Experimental ML Use Cases in Airlock](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~63466d407d10ef791492b491/pages/5614153902/LDR+Restricting+Production+Data+Access+for+Experimental+ML+Use+Cases+in+Airlock)

### 2.4 Security Guardrails

**Practical ML-specific security measures:**
- Zero trust for inputs: treat all prompts/uploads as untrusted
- Policy sandboxing: separate system prompts and tools; apply allow-lists for tool use
- Secrets hygiene: never put secrets in prompts or training data; use secrets manager
- Rate-limit & monitor: set quotas; alert on spikes, long prompts, unusual tool use
- Poisoning defences: vet data sources; checksum datasets; review fine-tune corpora
- SBOM & pinning: pin library versions; scan dependencies; sign models/artifacts
- Scope enforcement to owned services only
- Parameter validation and sane defaults
- Blast-radius checks before execution

Sources: [AI privacy, causality, security & fake content](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~70121eeecde7086e94a778d189b8b5d0a90f2/pages/5749575172/AI+privacy+causality+security+fake+content), [Implement safety guardrails and validations](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/JSRE-16846)

### 2.5 AI Risk Management Checklist

| Area | Potential Blocker | Mitigation Strategy |
|------|-------------------|---------------------|
| Model quality & safety | Hallucinations or unsafe outputs reach customers | Retrieval grounding, guardrails, toxicity/PII filters; confidence thresholds; feature flags and fast rollback |
| Data privacy & governance | Improper use of customer content | Contractual data handling; encrypt at rest/transit; redact PII pre-logging; access controls and audit trails |
| Fairness & bias | Biased outputs harm users or brands | Evaluation sets across sensitive attributes; fail gates on bias metrics; human review for edge cases |
| Security & abuse | Prompt injection, jailbreaks | Isolate tool execution; scope credentials; adversarial red-teaming; kill-switch |

Source: [AI Risk Management Checklist and Guidelines](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/aats/pages/6728253551/AI+Risk+Management+Checklist+and+Guidelines)

### 2.6 Compute Budget Governance

- GPU utilization monitoring (CPU, GPU, memory tracked via TeamServe/ML Lens)
- Cost attribution per model and per workload
- SageMaker auto-scaling tuning and budget thresholds in CI
- Resource audit reviewing predicted cloud spend before shipping to production

Source: [TeamServe <> ML Lens Operational Metrics Requirements](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~93171358/pages/6081093852/TeamServe+ML+Lens+Operational+Metrics+Requirements)

