## 5. Cross-Functional Collaboration Patterns

### 5.1 RACI Model for ML Projects

Based on the Core ML Team RACI Guide:

| Phase | Core ML | Analytics/DS | Engineering | PM | Experimentation |
|-------|---------|-------------|-------------|-----|-----------------|
| Problem Definition | I | R | — | A | — |
| Data & Feature Eng | R | A | — | — | — |
| Model Development | R | I | — | — | — |
| Feature Engineering (Prod) | R | A | — | — | — |
| Model Score Serving | R | I | R/C | — | — |
| Experiment Implementation | C | I/R | R | — | A |
| Experiment Launch | I | I | R | A | A |
| Experiment Measurement | C | R | I | I | A |
| Full Production Launch | I | I | R | — | — |

Source: [Core Machine Learning Team RACI Guide](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/1051522986/Core+Machine+Learning+Team+RACI+Guide)

### 5.2 MLE↔ Product Manager Collaboration

**Key interaction points:**
- Problem definition and customer pain point identification (PM drives, MLE informs)
- Success criteria alignment (primary/secondary KPIs agreed before experiment)
- Trade-off discussions on model complexity vs. development time
- Experiment result communication and launch decisions
- Feature prioritization when multiple ML initiatives compete

**Rituals:**
- Project poster creation (PM + MLE)
- Chopper reviews (bi-weekly ML Technical Advisory Group)
- Pre-analysis alignment (before experiment launch)
- Post-experiment result presentation

### 5.3 MLE ↔ Data Engineer Collaboration

**Key interaction points:**
- Pipeline reliability and data freshness SLAs
- Schema contracts and data quality checks
- Feature store materialization (MLFS)
- Upstream data source stability
- Data access provisioning and privacy compliance

**Common pain points (from internal research):**
- No mechanism for data quality checks on upstream tables
- No dedicated DE POC for ML teams
- Input pipeline should be conditional on upstream table quality

### 5.4 MLE ↔ Platform/Infra Team Collaboration

**Key interaction points:**
- Compute provisioning (GPU clusters, SageMaker endpoints, TeamServe)
- Deployment tooling (ML Studio workflows, model registry, deployment providers)
- Model serving infrastructure (scaling, latency optimization)
- Monitoring instrumentation (ML Lens integration)

**Collaboration model (from MLP retro):**
- Establish recurring collaboration sessions with customer teams
- Understand MLE workflows and pain points
- ML Platform takes customer-first approach, building tools while use cases are actively developed

Source: [MLP Retro Apr 2026](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6882381178/MLP+Retro+Apr+2026+Export+Apr+24+2026+07+05)

### 5.5 MLE ↔ Other MLEs (Peer Collaboration)

**Established processes:**
- **ML Technical Advisory Group:** Bi-weekly committee reviewing proposed models (implementation, evaluation, customer value)
- **Pairing sessions:** Walk through experimental code that might otherwise not be reviewed
- **Shared libraries:** Contributing common utilities to shared repos (devai-python-utils)
- **Standardized experiment documentation:** All experiment notebooks stored centrally
- **Model cards:** For any models intended for production
- **Data cards:** For all evaluation datasets

Source: [RFC: Machine Learning processes, rituals, and goals](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/jai/pages/5747870259/RFC+Machine+Learning+processes+rituals+and+goals), [2025/03ML Processes and Standards Session](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/4970135602/2025+03+ML+Processes+and+Standards+Session)

### 5.6 Cross-Product Architecture Forum

- Weekly sessions for cross-team collaboration on design and architecture
- Share: experiments/spikes, DACIs, integration patterns, data models, reusable components, standards/patterns, PIR learnings
- Presenters share reference materials by Tuesday before presentation
- Attendees review material beforehand for effective discussion

Source: [Cross-Product Collaboration Forum Agenda](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENTTCH/pages/3677467678/Cross-Product+Collaboration+Forum+Agenda)

