## 6. Common Failure Modes and Mitigation Strategies

### 6.1 Training-Serving Skew

**Description:** Online/offline consistency drift — when experiment layer configuration diverges between production and scraping/training, models trained on inconsistent data perform worse in production.

**Mitigations:**
- Ensure scraper configurations mirror production search configurations exactly
- Feature store serving architecture that guarantees online/offline consistency
- Integration tests comparing training-time feature values against production serving values
- Monitor for configuration drift between environments

Source: [3S - Operational Readiness Review](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SEARCH/pages/6722892863/3S+-+Operational+Readiness+Review)

### 6.2 Data Drift / Concept Drift

**Description:** Production data distributions diverge from training data distributions, degrading model performance. Detected across three dimensions: semantic drift, action drift, and data drift.

**Mitigations:**
- **Statistical hypothesis tests** (Kolmogorov-Smirnov) to determine if distributions are statistically different
- **Distance metrics** (Population Stability Index) to measure magnitude of distributional shift
- **Summary statistics** monitoring (mean, stddev, min, max) over time
- **Automated retraining triggers:** Time-based (every 15 days), metric-based (accuracy drops below threshold), data drift (patterns shift significantly)
- **ML Lens platform-level drift detection** automatically computing drift metrics for all MLFS-registered features

Sources: [[Design] ML Lens Platform Data Drift Detection](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6738511349/Design+ML+Lens+Platform+Data+Drift+Detection), [ML Observability - Feature Drift Migration to ML Lens](https://home.atlassian.com/o/2346a038-3c8c-498b-a79b-e7847859868d/s/a436116f-02ce-4520-8fbb-7301462a1674/project/ATLAS-124965)

### 6.3 Overfitting to Offline Metrics

**Description:** Model performs well on offline evaluation but fails to translate to production impact.

**Mitigations:**
- Correlate ML performance metrics with business metrics (D1-D6, PPF) to identify genuine model issues
- Use separate validation sets with future-dated data
- Catastrophic forgetting / drift checks: early stop if production val loss increases
- Compare LM-score distribution on production test set pre vs post fine-tune (KL-divergence under threshold)
- Run online A/B tests with adequate duration before full rollout

Source: [Spike - ML Observability - Thresholds for Alerting](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/4499900355/Spike+-+ML+Observability+-+Thresholds+for+Alerting)

### 6.4 Silent Model Degradation

**Description:** Model quality degrades gradually without triggering alerts. Per-placement signals drown in aggregate baselines.

**Mitigations:**
- **Per-placement alerting:** Encode placement into metric key → independent baselines → any single degradation fires alert
- **Layered alerting:** Drift alert + liveness alert in the same config
- **Phase-aware thresholds:** Tighter for production, looser for experiments
- **Automated health checks:** Continuous health checks for model updates, prompt drift, retrieval drift, infrastructure issues

Source: [Per-Placement Alerting at Scale for KYC ML Observability](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/KYC/pages/6967787922/Per-Placement+Alerting+at+Scale+for+KYC+ML+Observability)

### 6.5 Feature Store Staleness

**Description:** Feature data freshness exceeds acceptable thresholds, causing models to operate on stale data.

**Mitigations:**
- **Feature health metrics:** freshness, drift, null rates, distribution shifts
- **Infra health metrics:** materialization latency, job failures, online/offline consistency
- **Alerts when:** data freshness exceeds thresholds, distribution deviates beyond configured tolerances, materialization jobs fail or lag
- **No-data threshold alerting:** Alert if no data received within2× expected ingestion interval

Source: [How to productionise a Feature Service](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6157554821/How+to+productionise+a+Feature+Service)

### 6.6 GPU OOM During Training

**Description:** CUDA out-of-memory errors during multi-GPU distributed training, often confused with other failure types.

**Mitigations:**
- Batch/right-sizing and allocator tuning (`PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True`)
- Cache hygiene and safer defaults for large-memory pressure paths
- Distinguish hardware faults from software bugs:
  - ECC error: random timing, single rank affected, retry on different machine
  - DDP desync: reproducible at epoch/validation boundaries, all ranks report timeout
- Fresh single-GPU rank-0 trainer for post-training evaluation
- Quality gates rejecting jobs when failed record percentage exceeds threshold

Source: [Phase 9: Multi-GPU DDP for Model/Data Expansion](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020d90617ddcbda4dd992fbd2ae3e7ff2da/pages/6598080826/Phase+9+Multi-GPU+DDP+for+Model+Data+Expansion)

### 6.7 Reproducibility Failures

**Description:** Unable to reproduce past experiments or training results.

**Mitigations:**
- **Code versioning:** All code in Bitbucket repositories
- **Experiment tracking:** MLflow for logging parameters, metrics, artifacts
- **Naming conventions and tagging standards** for searchable experiments
- **Data versioning:** Source table versioning in Databricks
- **Containerization:** Docker/MSP for consistent inference environments
- **Model cards** for any models intended for production
- **Data cards** for all evaluation datasets
- **Workflow descriptors** (YAML) capturing all module configurations

Source: [MLOPs@CoreML Long Term Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202089f42605e1d342df8e8011fe153d216f/pages/5783505356/MLOPs+CoreML+Long+Term+Plan)

### 6.8 A/B Test Interpretation Errors

**Description:** Incorrect conclusions from experiment results due to statistical errors, insufficient sample size, or confounding factors.

**Mitigations:**
- Pre-analysis to confirm traffic lane, sample size, and run time
- KS tests to check statistical difference in distributions
- Separate experiment and production alerting with appropriate thresholds
- Decision logs documenting all experiment decisions and their impact
- Go/no-go decision frameworks (p-values, practical significance)
- Dedicated ML Technical Advisory Group reviewing experiment designs

Sources: [NBP Experiment ML Checklist](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DTIE/pages/5662721652/NBP+Experiment+ML+Checklist), [2025/03 ML Processes and Standards Session](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/4970135602/2025+03+ML+Processes+and+Standards+Session)

### 6.9 Technical Debt Accumulation in ML Systems

**Description:** Growing complexity from ad-hoc solutions, duplicated infrastructure, undocumented models, and inconsistent tooling.

**Mitigations:**
- **Standardized MLOps stack:** Reduce duplicated infrastructure efforts
- **Feature-gate lifecycle audit + cleanup:** Remove stale feature flags
- **Module development framework:** Structured modules vs. ad-hoc Python scripts
- **Shared libraries:** Prevent writing custom utilities that already exist
- **Regular processes and standards sessions** to align team practices
- **Documentation requirements:** Maintaining setup docs so anyone can run code locally
- **Anti-regression strategies:** Protocol locks, structured action contracts, post-write state sync

Sources: [2025/03 ML Processes and Standards Session](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/4970135602/2025+03+ML+Processes+and+Standards+Session), [Anti-Regression Strategies](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020a67732ba26ef4aafbc4b8d28ca2a8298/pages/6657442438/Anti-Regression+Strategies)

### 6.10 Infrastructure & Platform Failure Modes

| Failure Mode | Frequency | Mitigation |
|-------------|-----------|------------|
| Databricks UC connection failure | 35/72 failed jobs | Token refresh; network policy audit; circuit breakers |
| High record failure rate (>threshold) | 14/72 failed jobs | Quality gate rejects job; investigate per-record errors |
| SageMaker cold start lag (3-8 min) | Per-scaling event | Preemptive scaling; longer timeouts during cold starts |
| Vegas limiter saturation from bursty traffic | Periodic | ML Studio rate limiting; Vegas config tuning |
| UCT minting failure (id-gatekeeper down) | Rare | Retry at ML Studio level; circuit breaker |

Source: [ML Fabric Capabilities and their Alerts](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/6536338411/ML+Fabric+Capabilities+and+their+Alerts)

