## 7. Communication Norms and Documentation Standards

### 7.1 Experiment Documentation Standards

**Standardized template (from internal practices):**
- **Problem statement** — In brief paragraph
- **Hypothesis** — Assumption taken to solve the problem statement
- **Impact/Outcome** — If experiment goes to production, or learnings/decisions for future
- **Description** — Bullet points/paragraph
- **Dataset Used:** Source + Attributes
- **Metrics:** How this helps evaluate hypothesis/quality/business outcome
- **Design/Flow/mindmap diagrams**
- **Execution Steps**
- **Results:** metrics, trackers, charts/graphs, observations
- **Alternatives considered**
- **Notebook links** (source code, Databricks notebooks, dashboards)
- **Conclusion**
- **References**

Source: [ML Experiments - Documentation Template](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ITSOL/pages/4247330970/ML+Experiments+-+Documentation+Template)

### 7.2 Model Decision Logs

**Decision log structure (from Growth team practices):**
- **Decision:** What was decided
- **Status:** Pending / Accepted / Decided
- **Drivers:** Who drove the decision
- **Outcome:** What happened as a result
- **Impact:** Team impact (Low/Medium/High) + Experiment impact (Low/Medium/High) with details

**Key principles:**
- Should inform engineering and measurement approaches
- Should be a reference, not a discussion forum
- Clarity provided should be written back to Project Poster immediately
- Avoid turning into discussion forums that spawn ambiguity

Source: [Decision Log templates](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/Growth/pages/4757324054/Decision+Log+GRW-1427)

### 7.3 Handoff Protocols: Exploration → Productionization

**Three-document repository per model (from ML Technical Advisory Group proposal):**

1. **Ideation Document:**
   - Customer pain point
   - Datasets to use
   - Privacy concerns
   - Proposed model implementation

2. **Chopper Review Document (requires approval from ML committee):**
   - Links to central dashboards regarding model evals online/offline
   - Links to code locations
   - Links to datasets used
   - Explanation of models used

3. **Production Documentation:**
   - Model card (purpose, data, limits, fairness results)
   - Deployment configuration
   - Monitoring setup
   - Runbooks

Source: [RFC: Machine Learning processes, rituals, and goals](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/jai/pages/5747870259/RFC+Machine+Learning+processes+rituals+and+goals)

### 7.4 Standards Agreed by ML Teams (from Processes & Standards Session)

**"Start" items (team agreements):**
- Standardizing experiment documentation in Confluence
- Regular pairing sessions to walk through experimental code
- Contributing common utilities to shared libraries
- Storing all experiment notebooks centrally
- Logging data at designated locations
- Writing tests for even private repos
- Developing model cards for production models
- Developing data cards for all evaluation datasets
- Maintaining setup documentation so anyone can run code locally
- Writing reproducible Jupyter notebooks
- Sharing Loom video recordings + documentation

**"Stop" items:**
- Requiring push to main branch to run offline experiments
- Writing custom utilities that already exist in shared libraries
- Keeping experiment results in personal notebooks/local files not in git/cloud
- Having file limitations that restrict storage of large data/model files

Source: [2025/03 ML Processes and Standards Session](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/AIDO/pages/4970135602/2025+03+ML+Processes+and+Standards+Session)

