  5 Tools & Technologies — core vs secondary tools table, plus a Tech Stack &
    Codebase Context subsection with 6 codebase categories and 5 architectural
    patterns.
  6 Standard Operating Procedures — three concrete SOPs (greenfield-to-prod,
    incident response with quantified escalation thresholds,
    scheduled/triggered retrain).
  7 Collaboration & Communication — RACI table, cross-functional patterns,
    reporting structure for an AI employee, async-first communication norms.
  8 Success Metrics & KPIs — performance, operational, business, velocity,
    plus AI-specific quality bar; targets and cadences specified.
  9 Challenges & Mitigation — separated into technical / organizational /
    AI-MLE-specific.
 10 AI-Specific Work Philosophy — elevated standards from removed human
    limitations, plus an explicit guardrails matrix (Always Approval-gated /
    Reviewed / Autonomous / Hard halts / Weekly oversight).
 11 Day-One Readiness — tool access list, documents to ingest, and a graded
    4-week ramp of demonstration tasks.

Internal consistency was preserved (tools mentioned in §5 are referenced in §6
SOPs and §11 access list; autonomy taxonomy used in §2 is reused in §6 and
§10). Where worker outputs conflicted (human-centric meeting cadence,
onboarding ramp assumptions), the AI-native framing was preferred per the
breakdown's aggregation guidance.


